    explanation: "beginaligned &text  \\ &beginaligned (a)       T(n) & =T(n-1)+1 \\ & =T(n-2)+1+1 \\ & =T(n-k)+k             [n-k=1, k=n-1]\\ & =T(1)+n-1 \\ T(n) & =n endaligned\\ & endaligned    beginaligned(b)        & T(n)=2 T(fracn2)+1 \\ & f(n)=1, n^log _b^a=n endaligned  Master theorems case (i)   beginaligned             & T(n)=θ(n) \\\\(c)      & T(n)=2 T(fracn2)+n \\ & f(n)=n, n^log _b^a=n endaligned  Master theorems case (ii) applicable   beginaligned T(n) & =θ(n · log n) \\\\(d)    T(n) & =T(n-1)+n \\ & =T(n-2)+(n-1)+n \\ & =T(n-3)+(n-2)+(n-1)+n \\ & =T(1)+2+3+ldots . .+(n-1)+n \\ T(n) & =fracn(n+1)2=θ(n^2) endaligned"
