    explanation: "The basic block is:  - t_1 = a + b - t_2 = c + d - t_3 = e - t_2 - t_4 = t_1 - t_3  Optimal code:  1. ```c MOV a, R1 ``` 2. ```c ADD b, R1 ``` 3. ```c MOV R1, t1 ``` 4. ```c MOV c, R1 ``` 5. ```c ADD d, R1 ``` 6. ```c MOV R1, t2 ``` 7. ```c MOV e, R1 ``` 8. ```c SUB t2, R1 ``` 9. ```c MOV R1, t3 ``` 10. ```c MOV t1, R1 ``` 11. ```c SUB t3, R1 ``` 12. ```c MOV R1, t4 ```  This requires 6 MOV (memory to register) and 6 MOV (register to memory) instructions. However, we can optimize.  1. ```c MOV a, R1 ``` 2. ```c ADD b, R1 ``` 3. ```c MOV R1, t1 ``` 4. ```c MOV c, R2 ``` 5. ```c ADD d, R2 ``` 6. ```c SUB R2, R1 ``` 7. ```c MOV e, R2 ``` 8. ```c SUB R1, R2 ``` 9. ```c MOV R1, t4 ```  Minimum MOV instructions = 6 Quick Tip Eliminate redundant loads by keeping intermediate results in registers until needed."
