    type: "MCQ", marks: 1,
    question: "A 20 Kbps satellite link has a propagation delay of 400 ms. The transmitter employs the \"go back n ARQ\" scheme with n set to 10. Assuming that each frame is 100 byte long, what is the maximum data rate possible?",
    image: null,
    options: ["5 Kbps", "10 Kbps", "15 Kbps", "20 Kbps"],
    answer: "10 Kbps",
    explanation: "Derivation The maximum data rate (throughput) in a Go-Back-N (GBN) ARQ protocol is determined by the window size and the Round Trip Time (RTT).  Given data: Bandwidth (B) = 20text Kbps = 20,000text bps Propagation delay (t_p) = 400text ms = 0.4text s Window size (N) = 10 Frame size (L) = 100text bytes = 800text bits First, calculate the transmission time (t_t) for one frame:    t_t = fracLB = frac80020,000 = 0.04text s = 40text ms    The total cycle time to send a window and get the first ACK is approximately the Round Trip Time (RTT):    T_total = t_t + 2t_p = 40 + 2(400) = 840text ms    The maximum amount of data the sender can transmit in one full cycle is restricted by the window size N:    textData per cycle = N × L = 10 × 800 = 8000text bits    Calculating the exact maximum data rate:    textThroughput = fracN × Lt_t + 2t_p = frac8000text bits840text ms = 9.52text Kbps    In classic networking problems, examiners often approximate the total cycle time by ignoring the small transmission time in the denominator (T_total approx 2t_p = 800text ms):    textApprox Throughput = frac8000text bits800text ms = 10text Kbps  10text Kbps exactly matches Option B. Common Trap Aspirants often calculate a = t_p/t_t = 10 and use the efficiency formula eta = fracN1+2a = frac1021, giving 9.52text Kbps. When this isn't an option, they mistakenly assume N is too small and default to the full 20text Kbps link speed, ignoring the ARQ bottleneck. AIR-1 Insight When a calculated throughput (like 9.52text Kbps) is very close to a clean integer option (like 10text Kbps), it indicates the examiner simplified the equation by dropping t_t from the denominator. Recognize this approximation to secure the mark. Quick Tip Check bandwidth utilization"
