    type: "NAT", marks: 2,
    question: "For a host machine that uses the token bucket algorithm for congestion control, the token bucket has a capacity of 1 megabyte and the maximum output rate is 20 megabytes per second. Tokens arrive at a rate to sustain output at a rate of 10megabytes per second. The  token bucket is currently full and the machine needs to send 12megabytes of data. The minimum time required to transmit the data is _____seconds.",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "1.1",
    explanation: "Let C be the bucket capacity, M be the maximum output rate, rho be the token arrival rate, and S be the total data to send. C = 1 text MB, M = 20 text MB/s, rho = 10 text MB/s, S = 12 text MB. The maximum time t for which the bucket can transmit at the peak rate M before emptying is given by: C + rho t = M t implies 1 + 10t = 20t implies 10t = 1 implies t = 0.1 text s. Data sent during this burst = M × t = 20 × 0.1 = 2 text MB. Remaining data to send = S - 2 = 12 - 2 = 10 text MB. Once the bucket is empty, the data can only be transmitted at the token arrival rate rho (10 MB/s). Time required to send the remaining data = frac10 text MB10 text MB/s = 1 text s. Total minimum time = Burst time + Remaining time = 0.1 + 1 = 1.1 text seconds. Quick Tip When bucket is full, send at max rate until tokens deplete, then rely on token arrival rate."
