    question: "The values of parameters for the Stop-and-Wait ARQ protocol are as given below: Bit rate of the transmission channel = 1Mbps Propagation delay from sender to receiver = 0.75 ms Time to process a frame = 0.25ms Number of bytes in the information frame =1980 Number of bytes in the acknowledge frame = 20 Number of overhead bytes in the information frame = 20 Assume that there are no transmission errors. Then the transmission efficiency ( expressed in percentage) of the Stop-and - Wait ARQ protocol for the above parameters is _________( correct to 2 decimal places)",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "86.5 to 89.5",
    explanation: "Calculate transmission time of the information frame (T_f): - Information frame size: 1980 + 20 = 2000 bytes - T_f = frac2000 × 81 × 10^6 = 0.016 s = 16 ms Calculate transmission time of the acknowledgment frame (T_a): - Acknowledgment frame size: 20 × 8 bits - T_a = frac20 × 81 × 10^6 = 0.00016 s = 0.16 ms Calculate total time for one cycle (T): - T = T_f + T_a + 2 × T_p + 2 × T_proc - T_p = 0.75 ms, T_proc = 0.25 ms - T = 16 + 0.16 + 2 × 0.75 + 2 × 0.25 = 16 + 0.16 + 1.5 + 0.5 = 18.16 ms Calculate efficiency (eta): - eta = fracT_fT = frac1618.16 = 0.8810572687 - eta × 100 = 88.10572687 approx 88.11 Quick Tip Convert all times to milliseconds first; then efficiency = (payload bits / total bits transmitted in one cycle) ×100."
