    question: "In a RSA cryptosystem a participant A uses two prime numbers p=13 and q=17 to generate her public and private keys. If the public key of A is 35. Then the private key of A is __________.",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "11",
    explanation: "p = 13, q = 17. n = p × q = 13 × 17 = 221. Euler's totient φ(n) = (p-1)(q-1) = 12 × 16 = 192. Public key e = 35. Private key d is the modular multiplicative inverse of e pmodφ(n), i.e., ed equiv 1 pmod192. 35d equiv 1 pmod192. Using Extended Euclidean Algorithm: 192 = 5 × 35 + 17 35 = 2 × 17 + 1 1 = 35 - 2 × 17 1 = 35 - 2 × (192 - 5 × 35) 1 = 35 - 2 × 192 + 10 × 35 1 = 11 × 35 - 2 × 192 So, d equiv 11 pmod192. The private key is 11. Quick Tip When e and φ(n) are small, quickly check multiples of φ(n) added to 1 until divisible by e."
