    answer: "16",
    explanation: "Cache Parameters - Cache size: 32 text KB = 32768 text bytes - Block size: 128 text bytes - Array size: 512 × 512 × 8 text bytes - Elements/block: 128/8 = 16 P1 (Row-major) - M1 = 512 × (512/16) = 512 × 32 = 16384 - M1 = 512 * 32 = 16384 P2 (Column-major) - M2 = 512 × 512 = 262144 - M2 = 512 * 512 = 262144 Direct Mapped - M1 = 512 * 32 = 16384 - M2 = 512 * 1024/128 = 4096 - M1/M2 = 16384/1024 = 16 Quick Tip Row‑major layout means sequential accesses hit the same block; column‑major accesses cause a miss every new row."
