    answer: "D_2 > D > D_1",
    explanation: "Let t be the time for the fixed-point unit in design D.  - Design D: T_D = 0.8t + 0.2(2t) = 1.2t - Design D_1: T_D_1 = 0.8(1.3t) + 0.2(1.4t) = 1.04t + 0.28t = 1.32t - Design D_2: T_D_2 = 0.8(0.6t) + 0.2(2.2t) = 0.48t + 0.44t = 0.92t  Since 0.92t < 1.2t < 1.32t, we have D_2 < D < D_1. Therefore, D_2 > D > D_1. Quick Tip Factor out the base cycle t; the design with the smallest coefficient of t is the fastest."
