    answer: "14020",
    explanation: "Problem Setup  - We are given a disk pack with the following characteristics:   - Seek time: 4 ms   - Rotational speed: 10000 RPM   - Sectors per track: 600   - Bytes per sector: 512 - A file of 2000 sectors is stored on the disk. - Every sector access requires a seek operation. - The average rotational latency is half the time for one complete rotation. - We need to calculate the total time required to read the entire file. Calculate Rotation Time  - First, calculate the time for one complete rotation:   -   textRotational Speed = 10000 text rotations per minute    -   textTime for one rotation = frac60 text seconds10000 text rotations = 0.006 text seconds = 6 text ms  Calculate Average Rotational Latency  - The average rotational latency is half of the time for one rotation:   -   textAverage Rotational Latency = frac6 text ms2 = 3 text ms  Calculate Time Per Sector Access  - Each sector access requires a seek and experiences rotational latency:   -   textTime per sector access = textSeek Time + textAverage Rotational Latency    -   textTime per sector access = 4 text ms + 3 text ms = 7 text ms  Calculate Total Time  - The file contains 2000 sectors, and each sector access takes 7 ms:   -   textTotal Time = textTime per sector access × textNumber of sectors    -   textTotal Time = 7 text ms × 2000 = 14000 text ms  Conclusion  - The total time needed to read the entire file is 14000 ms. Quick Tip Half‑rotation time = 0.5 × (60 000 ms ÷ RPM)."
