    type: "NAT", marks: 1,
    question: "A 32-bit wide main memory unit with a capacity of 1 GB is built using 256M x 4-bit DRAM chips. The number of rows of memory cells in the DRAM chip is 2^14 . The time taken to perform one refresh operation is 50 nanoseconds. The refresh period is 2 milliseconds. The percentage (rounded to the closest integer) of the time available for performing the memory read/write operations in the main memory unit is __________.",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "59 to 60",
    explanation: "Memory Organization  - The main memory has a capacity of 1 GB, which is 1 × 2^30 bytes. Since it is 32-bit wide, the number of memory locations is:     frac1 × 2^30 text bytes4 text bytes/location = 2^28 text locations   - Each DRAM chip has a size of 256M x 4-bit, which is 256 × 2^20 × 4 bits = 2^8 × 2^20 × 4 bits = 2^30 bits = 2^27 bytes.  - Number of DRAM chips required:     frac1 × 2^30 text bytes2^27 text bytes/chip = 2^3 = 8 text chips   - Since the memory is 32-bit wide and each chip provides 4 bits, we need 8 chips to form the 32-bit word. DRAM Refresh  - Number of rows in each DRAM chip = 2^14.  - Refresh period = 2 ms = 2 × 10^-3 seconds.  - Time to perform one refresh operation = 50 ns = 50 × 10^-9 seconds.  - Number of refresh operations required in each refresh period = Number of rows = 2^14.  - Total time taken for refresh operations in each refresh period:  2^14 × 50 × 10^-9 text seconds = 16384 × 50 × 10^-9 text seconds = 819200 × 10^-9 text seconds = 819.2 × 10^-6 text seconds = 0.8192 × 10^-3 text seconds = 0.8192 text ms   Calculation of Available Time Percentage  - Percentage of time taken for refresh operations:     frac0.8192 text ms2 text ms × 100 = 40.96 \\%   - Percentage of time available for read/write operations:  100 \\% - 40.96 \\% = 59.04 \\%   - Rounding to the closest integer, the percentage of time available for performing the memory read/write operations in the main memory unit is 59%. Quick Tip Memory refresh overhead is a common concept in computer architecture. Focus on time percentages."
