    type: "NAT", marks: 1,
    question: "A direct mapped cache memory of 1 MB has a block size of 256 bytes. The cache has an access time of 3 ns and a hit rate of 94%. During a cache miss, it takes 20 ns to bring the first word of a block from the main memory, while each subsequent word takes 5 ns. The word size is 64 bits. The average memory access time in ns (round off to 1 decimal place) is______.",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "13.5",
    explanation: "Block size = 256 bytes. Word size = 64 bits = 8 bytes. Number of words per block = 256 / 8 = 32 words. Miss penalty is the time to transfer the entire block. Transfer time = Time for first word + Time for remaining 31 words. Miss penalty = 20 text ns + 31 × 5 text ns = 20 + 155 = 175 text ns. Hit time = 3 ns. Hit rate = 0.94. Miss rate = 0.06. Average Memory Access Time (AMAT) = Hit time + Miss rate × Miss penalty. AMAT = 3 text ns + 0.06 × 175 text ns = 3 + 10.5 = 13.5 text ns. Quick Tip No quick tip available"
