    question: "A hash table with ten buckets with one slot per bucket is shown in the following figure. The symbols S1 to S7 initially entered using a hashing function with linear probing. The maximum number of comparisons needed in searching an item that is not present is beginarray|l|l| hline 0 & text  S7  \\ hline 1 & text  S1  \\ hline 2 & \\ hline 3 & text  S4  \\ hline 4 & text  S2  \\ hline 5 & text   \\ hline 6 & text  S5  \\ hline 7 & \\ hline 8 & text  S6  \\ hline 9 & text  S3  \\ hline endarray",
