    explanation: "Statement C is FALSE. It is not always possible to decompose a relation into BCNF while preserving both losslessness and functional dependencies. Dependency preservation may be lost (e.g., when a dependency spans the candidate keys). 3NF decomposition guarantees both. Quick Tip If a decomposition must keep all functional dependencies, BCNF often fails this test."
