    explanation: "Query Analysis - Goal: Find last names and hire dates of latest hires in departments with location ID 1700. - Subquery:    SELECT dept\\_id, MAX(hire\\_date) FROM employees JOIN departments USING(dept\\_id) WHERE location\\_id = 1700 GROUP BY dept\\_id    finds the latest hire date for each department at location 1700. - Main query:    SELECT last\\_name, hire\\_date FROM employees WHERE (dept\\_id, hire\\_date) IN (subquery)    selects employees matching those (department, hire date) pairs. - Result: Correctly returns the last name and hire date of the latest hires. Quick Tip Use EXISTS with a correlated subquery to avoid pairwise comparison pitfalls."
