    answer: "The database system is both deadlock-free and starvation- free.",
    explanation: "Algorithm Analysis - If TS(T_1) < TS(T_2): T_1 waits; deadlock-free. - If TS(T_1) > TS(T_2): T_2 killed and restarted; deadlock-free. - Starvation is avoided since killed transactions are restarted. Quick Tip Use elimination: if TS(T1)<TS(T2) no wait, if TS(T1)>TS(T2) kill T2—no deadlock, no starvation."
