    question: "Consider the following circuit. The flip-flops are positive edge triggered D FFs. Each state is designated as a two-bit string Q0Q1. Let the initial state be 00. The state transition sequence is ```c // Define the state transition function void state_transition(int Q0, int Q1, int* next_state) {     *next_state = (Q1 << 1) | Q0; }  // Define the D flip-flop function void d_flip_flop(int D, int* Q) {     *Q = D; }  int main() {     int Q0, Q1, next_state;      // Initialize the state     Q0 = 0;     Q1 = 0;      // Perform state transitions     state_transition(Q0, Q1, &next_state);     printf(\"Next state: %d%d \", next_state >> 1, next_state & 1);      // Update the state     Q0 = next_state >> 1;     Q1 = next_state & 1;      // Perform state transitions again     state_transition(Q0, Q1, &next_state);     printf(\"Next state: %d%d \", next_state >> 1, next_state & 1);      return 0; } ```",
