    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "250",
    explanation: "#  ## Logic  - In a ripple counter, each flip-flop divides the frequency of the preceding flip-flop by 2. - For a 4-bit ripple counter, the last flip-flop (4th flip-flop) divides the original clock frequency by 2^4 = 16. - Therefore, f_last = fracf_clock16 Calculation - Given that the period of the waveform at the last flip-flop (T_last) is 64 microseconds, we can calculate the frequency of the last flip-flop (f_last):    f_last = frac1T_last = frac164 × 10^-6 = frac10^664 text Hz - Now, we can find the original clock frequency (f_clock):    f_clock = 16 × f_last = 16 × frac10^664 = frac10^64 = 250 × 10^3 text Hz = 250 text kHz    Therefore, the frequency of the ripple counter is 250 kHz. Quick Tip Use f_last = frac1T_last to find the frequency of the last flip-flop"
