    question: "An operating system uses shortest remaining time first scheduling algorithm for pre-emptive scheduling of processes. Consider the following set of processes with their arrival times and CPU burst times (in milliseconds): The average waiting time (in milliseconds) of the processes is _________.",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "5.5",
    explanation: "**Shortest Remaining Time First (SRTF) Scheduling Analysis**  **1. Gantt Chart Development:** The execution order based on the minimum remaining burst time at each arrival: - [0-2]: P1 (Remaining: 10) - [2-6]: P2 (Finishes at 6) - [6-12]: P3 (Finishes at 12) - [12-17]: P4 (Finishes at 17) - [17-27]: P1 (Finishes at 27)  **2. Calculation Table:** \\[ \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|} \\hline \\text{Process} & \\text{AT} & \\text{BT} & \\text{CT} & \\text{TAT} & \\text{WT} \\\\ \\hline P1 & 0 & 12 & 27 & 27 & 15 \\\\ \\hline P2 & 2 & 4 & 6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ \\hline P3 & 3 & 6 & 12 & 9 & 3 \\\\ \\hline P4 & 8 & 5 & 17 & 9 & 4 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \\]  **3. Final Computation:** \\[ \\text{Total Waiting Time} = 15 + 0 + 3 + 4 = 22 \\text{ ms} \\] \\[ \\text{Average Waiting Time} = \\frac{22}{4} = \\mathbf{5.5 \\text{ ms}} \\]  Quick Tip Sum up waiting times and divide by the number of processes to find the average waiting time."
