    answer: "SRTF = 6, NP-SJF = 7.5",
    explanation: "Part 1: Preemptive SRTF  Given:  | Process | Arrival Time | Burst Time | |---|---:|---:| | A | 0 | 10 | | B | 2 | 6 | | C | 4 | 3 | | D | 6 | 7 |  #Gantt Chart  At t=0, only A is available.  A executes from 0 to 2.  Remaining time of A:  10-2=8  At t=2, B arrives with burst time 6.  Since 6<8, B preempts A.  B executes from 2 to 4.  Remaining time of B:  6-2=4  At t=4, C arrives with burst time 3.  Since 3<4, C preempts B.  C executes from 4 to 7 and completes.  At t=6, D arrives, but C has only 1 unit remaining, so C continues.  At t=7:  - A remaining = 8 - B remaining = 4 - D remaining = 7  Therefore, B executes next.  B executes from 7 to 11 and completes.  At t=11:  - A remaining = 8 - D remaining = 7  Therefore, D executes before A.  D executes from 11 to 18 and completes.  Finally, A executes from 18 to 26.  Thus:  0-2:A | 2-4:B | 4-7:C | 7-11:B | 11-18:D | 18-26:A  #Completion Times  CT_A=26  CT_B=11  CT_C=7  CT_D=18  #Waiting Times  For A:  WT_A=26-0-10=16  For B:  WT_B=11-2-6=3  For C:  WT_C=7-4-3=0  For D:  WT_D=18-6-7=5  Therefore,  WT_avg=frac16+3+0+54  =frac244  =6  Hence,  SRTF=6  Part 2: Non-Preemptive SJF  At t=0, only A is available, so A executes completely.  A executes from 0 to 10.  At t=10, the available processes are:  - B: burst 6 - C: burst 3 - D: burst 7  The shortest is C.  Therefore:  A:0-10  C:10-13  B:13-19  D:19-26  #Completion Times  CT_A=10  CT_C=13  CT_B=19  CT_D=26  #Waiting Times  For A:  WT_A=10-0-10=0  For B:  WT_B=19-2-6=11  For C:  WT_C=13-4-3=6  For D:  WT_D=26-6-7=13  Therefore,  WT_avg=frac0+11+6+134  =frac304  =7.5  Hence,  NPtext-SJF=7.5  ## Official Answer Check  The official GATE 2024 CSE Set 2 answer is:  boxedtextB. SRTF=6, textNP-SJF=7.5  This matches the above derivation.  ## Final Answer  boxedtextB. SRTF=6, textNP-SJF=7.5  ## 💡 Quick Tip  The important point in SRTF is to re-check the remaining times whenever a new process arrives.  At t=11, A has 8 units remaining but D has only 7 units remaining, so D must execute before A. This is the step that is easy to miss."
