    question: "Consider a memory management system that uses a page size of ```c #define PAGE_SIZE 2048 ``` 2 mathrm~KB . Assume that both the physical and virtual addresses start from 0. Assume that the pages ```c #define PAGE_0 0 #define PAGE_1 1 #define PAGE_2 2 #define PAGE_3 3 ``` 0,1,2 , and 3 are stored ∈ the page frames ```c #define FRAME_1 1 #define FRAME_3 3 #define FRAME_2 2 #define FRAME_0 0 ``` 1,3,2 , and 0 , respectively. The physical address (in decimal format) corresponding to the virtual address 2500 (in decimal format) is ____",
