    id: "PYQ2995", year: 2025, subject: "Operating Systems", topic: "Memory Management",
    type: "NAT", marks: 2,
    question: "In optimal page replacement algorithm, information about all future page references is available to the operating system (OS). A modification of the optimal page replacement algorithm is as follows: The OS correctly predicts only up to next 4 page references (including the current page) at the time of allocating a frame to a page. A process accesses the pages in the following order of page numbers: 1, 3, 2, 4, 2, 3, 1, 2, 4, 3, 1, 4. If the system has three memory frames that are initially empty, the number of page faults that will occur during execution of the process is _________. (Answer in integer)",
    image: null,
    options: [],
    answer: "6",
    explanation: "Problem Statement We are given a page reference string and a modified optimal page replacement algorithm with a limited lookahead. The goal is to determine the number of page faults that occur during the execution of a process. Given Information  - Page reference string: 1, 3, 2, 4, 2, 3, 1, 2, 4, 3, 1, 4 - Number of memory frames: 3 (initially empty) - Lookahead window size: 4 (current page + next 3 pages) Algorithm The modified optimal page replacement algorithm works as follows:  - When a page fault occurs, the operating system (OS) looks ahead at the next 4 page references (including the current one). - If any of the pages currently in memory are *not* referenced in the lookahead window, the page that is not referenced is replaced. - If multiple pages satisfy the above condition, the page with the farthest next use is replaced. This essentially means we prioritize removing the page that won't be used for the longest time within the lookahead window. - If all pages in memory *are* referenced within the lookahead window, then the page within the current frame, whose *next* usage is farthest away in future is replaced. The lookahead window helps in making this decision. Step-by-step Execution We can trace the execution of the algorithm with the given page reference string and memory frames:  1.  Page 1: Frames are empty. Load 1. Frames: [1]. Page fault. 2.  Page 3: Frames: [1]. Load 3. Frames: [1, 3]. Page fault. 3.  Page 2: Frames: [1, 3]. Load 2. Frames: [1, 3, 2]. Page fault. 4.  Page 4: Frames: [1, 3, 2]. Lookahead: 2, 4, 2, 3. 1 is not in the lookahead. Replace 1. Frames: [4, 3, 2]. Page fault. 5.  Page 2: Frames: [4, 3, 2]. Hit. 6.  Page 3: Frames: [4, 3, 2]. Hit. 7.  Page 1: Frames: [4, 3, 2]. Lookahead: 2, 3, 1, 2. 4 is not in the lookahead. Replace 4. Frames: [1, 3, 2]. Page fault. 8.  Page 2: Frames: [1, 3, 2]. Hit. 9.  Page 4: Frames: [1, 3, 2]. Lookahead: 4, 3, 1, 4. All are in the lookahead. 3 is used latest compared to 1 and 2. Replace 3. Frames: [1, 4, 2]. Page fault. 10. Page 3: Frames: [1, 4, 2]. Lookahead: 3, 1, 4. 2 is not in the lookahead. Replace 2. Frames: [1, 4, 3]. Page fault. 11. Page 1: Frames: [1, 4, 3]. Hit. 12. Page 4: Frames: [1, 4, 3]. Hit.Summary Table  | Step | Page | Frames (Before) | Action                                  | Frames (After) | Fault? | |------|------|-----------------|-----------------------------------------|----------------|--------| | 1    | 1    | []              | Load 1                               | [1]            | Yes    | | 2    | 3    | [1]             | Load 3                               | [1, 3]         | Yes    | | 3    | 2    | [1, 3]          | Load 2                               | [1, 3, 2]      | Yes    | | 4    | 4    | [1, 3, 2]       | Replace 1 (Lookahead: 2, 4, 2, 3) | [4, 3, 2]      | Yes    | | 5    | 2    | [4, 3, 2]       | Hit                                     | [4, 3, 2]      | No     | | 6    | 3    | [4, 3, 2]       | Hit                                     | [4, 3, 2]      | No     | | 7    | 1    | [4, 3, 2]       | Replace 4 (Lookahead: 2, 3, 1, 2) | [1, 3, 2]      | Yes    | | 8    | 2    | [1, 3, 2]       | Hit                                     | [1, 3, 2]      | No     | | 9    | 4    | [1, 3, 2]       | Replace 3 (Lookahead: 4, 3, 1, 4) | [1, 4, 2]      | Yes    | | 10   | 3    | [1, 4, 2]       | Replace 2 (Lookahead: 3, 1, 4)    | [1, 4, 3]      | Yes    | | 11   | 1    | [1, 4, 3]       | Hit                                     | [1, 4, 3]      | No     | | 12   | 4    | [1, 4, 3]       | Hit                                     | [1, 4, 3]      | No     | Result The total number of page faults is 6.     textNumber of page faults = 6  Quick Tip For the modified optimal page replacement algorithm, focus on the lookahead window to decide which page to replace. If a page is not referenced within the lookahead window, replace it. If all pages are referenced, replace the page with the farthest next use."
